Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for Next.js App Router

Summary:
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

Changes Made:

1. Package Installation:
   - Installed @vercel/analytics@2.0.1 using pnpm (project's package manager)
   - Updated package.json to include the new dependency
   - Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with the new package and its dependencies

2. Analytics Integration:
   - Modified app/src/app/layout.tsx to integrate analytics
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the body element of the root layout
   - Followed Next.js App Router best practices as specified in the documentation

3. Verification:
   - Build completed successfully with no errors
   - Linter passed with no errors
   - No test scripts were available in the project

Implementation Details:
The Analytics component was placed at the end of the body element in the root layout, which is the recommended location for Next.js App Router applications. This ensures the analytics script loads after the main content and tracks page views across the entire application.

The integration follows the framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router from the official Vercel documentation, ensuring the most up-to-date and correct implementation.

Next Steps:
To activate the analytics:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Monitor the Network tab for `/<unique-path>/view` requests to confirm tracking is working
